  "body": "Add a **\"Your first router part\"** guide page under `site/content/guide/` (router counterpart to `first-run.md` and sibling to #1905).\n\n## Content\n\n1. **Complete walkthrough on `Sienci AltMill` + `grblhal.cps`:**\n   - Choose `assets/machines/sienci-altmill-4x4.mch` and post with `assets/posts/grblhal.cps` (already shipped in CamCraft, with no dedicated guide page today).\n   - Commit one small demo project showing sheet stock setup, corner work offset (`G54`), flat end mill selection, `2D Contour` with holding tabs, `2D Pocket`, and `Drill`.\n   - Show simulation, cut order, common router refusals, and posting to `.nc`.\n2. **Shop-router workflow section (`RichAuto DSP A11`):**\n   - Document USB `FAT32` and `8.3` filename rules, checking `G Code Setup` (`AbsCntr = Off`), Z puck `C.A.D Thickness` touch-off, and single-tool file workflow for handheld DSP shop routers.\n3. **Navigation and images:**\n   - Link the page from the Getting started / Workflows sections in `site/content/guide/` and from the `## Router` section in `site/content/guide/machines.md`.\n   - List needed screenshots cleanly for #1902 (reproducible off-screen renders) once available.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Clean room: write original CamCraft guide text only. Cite public OEM controller manuals where needed. Never include Autodesk, HSMWorks, or third-party CAM material.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The committed demo project posts cleanly through `grblhal.cps` with zero refusals.\n- The guide page and `RichAuto DSP A11` section live under `site/content/guide/` and link from Getting started and `site/content/guide/machines.md`.\n- `zola build` passes with zero broken links.\n\nPart of #1907\n",
